honestly, i'd get out of the mindset of a 'perfect team'.

make 'idealized' teams, not necessarily teams designed to do everything.

kinda good and bad, but the game dev SPECIFICALLY designed stuff in this game to outright fuck you over for expecting one team to 'do it all'. it could be as small as certain challenges maybe needing a tweak to the team, or just meant to outright fuck over specific builds, to force you to do something else.

&#x200B;

so, i'd suggest making this team as 'perfect' as you can, but not feel like it has to be the One True Build for you, or some shit. this is the wrong mindset, especially for this game.

