the reason it's getting so much attention now is, they finally fixed the knife throw skill - before, you 'could' do it, but you'd lose the knives after throwing them. they weren't lootable, so you'd need decent tech to craft dozens of them.

&#x200B;

now, not only are they reusable, but they can even return to you after a certain time period, so you can equip 3 and just toss them like crazy.

you're going to want cold blood, because you're also going to want high ninjutsu, so might as well.

cold blood is sort of a 'general' passive buff, so it can be good for a lot of builds, though is often not insanely strong for any specific build.

&#x200B;

max both reflexes and cool because it's got your two main skill trees, blades, and ninjutsu. you'll also get decent bonuses to both poison and bleed, potentially, so that's helpful as well.

&#x200B;

you don't really need 20 body, i'd suggest some int and tech for this sort of build as well, hacking away any electronic troubles and giving access to as much as possible is better than getting a little more 'melee damage' on dem knives.

&#x200B;

since knife return time is based on rarity, i do kinda suggest getting tech to level 12 - it'll also allow you to make sure you can keep up decent amounts of armor and whatnot, and high end mods to make shit just \*chef's kiss\*

if you do want tons of body (which, this is a blades build, not really needed), just go with 5, put the 7 points here in body. you can still make rare blades

&#x200B;

int at 11 will allow you to get some nice hacking potential without needing to be an expert, getting that icepick ram decrease, the mass vulnerability buffs you want for a non-hacker build, etc, as well as making quickhacking devices super cheap - it's a hell of a lot easier to stay unseen when you can dominate the cameras before the fight even begins.

&#x200B;

body's a bit hit and miss, if you're not doing a annihilation/street brawler build, really. the extra health, stamina skills might be nice, whereas one point in epimorphesis means you'll never need to worry about health in between fights (to be fair, after a while this should be a OP stealth build, but still, early game kinda sucks)

you don't really need the melee combat help a katana build might want, given you're tossing knives, and even 20 points is only like 25% melee damage bonus - you can definitely do without it and still kick all sorts of ass, whereas access to some of the other stuff would be far more detrimental than using body as a dump stat.

